topics.description:
### @font-face
Register a font file and give it a family name:

```css
@font-face {
  font-family: "Brand";
  src: url("/fonts/brand.woff2") format("woff2"),
       url("/fonts/brand.woff") format("woff");
  font-weight: 400;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
body { font-family: "Brand", system-ui, sans-serif; }
```

### Formats
| Format | Use |
|---|---|
| `woff2` | best compression, supported everywhere modern - use this |
| `woff` | fallback |
| `ttf/otf` | legacy/desktop; the course demo used OpenType |

### font-display
- `swap`: show fallback immediately, swap when loaded (recommended).
- `optional`: use font only if it is available very quickly.
- `block`: invisible text up to ~3s (avoid).

### Performance tips
- Self-host and use `<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>` for the main font.
- Subset the font (only needed glyphs) with `unicode-range`.
- Limit weights/styles.
- Match fallback metrics with `size-adjust` to reduce layout shift.

### Variable fonts
One file contains a continuous range of axes (weight, width, slant, optical size).

```css
@font-face { font-family: "Inter VF"; src: url("inter-var.woff2") format("woff2"); font-weight: 100 900; }
h1 { font-weight: 650; font-variation-settings: "wdth" 110; }
```
Benefits: fewer files, fine-grained control, smooth weight animation on hover.

### Fallback stack
Always finish with a generic family so text stays readable if the font fails.

examples.code:
@font-face {
  font-family: "Urbanist";
  src: url("/fonts/urbanist-var.woff2") format("woff2");
  font-weight: 100 900;
  font-display: swap;
  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF;
}

