topics.description:
Two small projects that turn plain headings into animated text.

### 1. Text reveal
**Idea**: place a copy of the text on top of the original using `::before` with `content: "SUBSCRIBE..."`. The copy has a different color, `overflow: hidden` and a right border (the caret). Animate its **width** from 0 to 100% so the colored text appears to be typed or revealed.

Key lines:
```css
h1 { position: relative; }
h1::before {
  content: "SUBSCRIBE...";
  position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0;
  overflow: hidden; border-right: 2px solid #e9b824;
  animation: textreveal 2s linear infinite;
}
@keyframes textreveal { 0% { width: 0; } 50% { width: 100%; } 100% { width: 0; } }
```

### 2. Floating text
A heading with a soft **text-shadow** that rocks back and forth:

```css
h1 { text-shadow: -3px 10px 10px rgba(249,141,141,.2);
     animation: textfloating 1s linear infinite alternate; }
@keyframes textfloating { 0% { rotate: 15deg; } 50% { rotate: 0deg; } 100% { rotate: -15deg; } }
```

### Concepts used
Pseudo-elements, `overflow: hidden`, `position`, keyframes, `alternate` direction, text-shadow.

### Notes
Animating `width` triggers layout; it is fine for one headline. For many elements use `clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0)` -> `inset(0)` instead.

